<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#burushaski">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burushaski</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Burushaski language</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Burushaski is a language spoken in the Hunza, Nagar and Yasin valleys of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilgit-baltistan">Gilgit-Baltistan</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>. It is a language isolate, with no proven relationship to any other language. Its speakers, the Burusho, formed the population of the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of Hunza and Nagar.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/burushaski.jpg" alt="Burushaski" width="320" height="228" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ThatDohDude · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burushaski_in_Perso-Arabic.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
